This game does not have any fancy features like deep character customization, lots of perks and skills, non-linear story or revolutionary role-playing mechanic. But, come on, give it a chance!
So, what are pros and cons about playing "Mad Nords"?
+ it's funny. Yeah, you probably won't see anything extraordinaty, but I'm sure that this game will make you smile in the end of the hard week;
+ it has lots of... uhm... weird equipment you definitely haven't seen yet. Giant nail as an armor? Cheat scroll instead of sword? You personall accessory-dwarf? All these are quite common in the "Mad Nords";
+ it's not a Dragon age game, so you wont be saving the world... or would you? Maybe, you will, but your reasons to act will be simple and common for most of the people;
+ fighting system is both dynamic and easy-to-use. If you've played Deep Dungeons of Doom, you know, what I mean.
- lots of dungeons. Actually, it's a joke about those old-school RPGs where you had to spent hours in mines, caves etc. and it works for you if you like dungeons, but it totally didn't work for me;
- balance. If you don't know, how to pick the locks, you'll miss 80% of loot and some quests. And it's fine when you have other ways to earn money or to finish the quest, but most of the times you'll have only one option to end the quest. I've finished the early-access version of the game without buying anything except some healing poitions, so... maybe you don't really need money in this game;
- there is almost no difference in choosing necromancer or brut class cause you'll not get any extra content for that, nor you will have to change your way of playing. Yeah, your skill tree will be different, but there are only 5 skills in it.
Conclusion: play "Mad Nords" if you want to relax and have some fun playing a game, that does not try to f**k your brains with ultrahard meachincs and storyline.

I liked this visual novel quite a lot, but I wish it was longer. Basically, it’s about Brian, an American student living in Japan and we follow him as he learns more about the culture and makes new friends.
The glossary during the dialogues was useful, and both main heroines are cute and interesting. I understand that the game was made for a certain audience, but I get this feeling that they lost a chance to make it more “educational”. It goes from an interesting subject to fan service pretty fast in a few scenes, and that bothered me a bit. Also, there’s the endings;
7/10. I liked the concept, the art style is really pretty, the songs are catchy. But as I already said, I think they could’ve done a bit more here. Also, the story gets fast at some point, one day you’re celebrating Halloween, and then suddenly it’s Christmas and it goes on. I recommend getting this title on a sale if you want a light story to read.
